    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0334" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115 Standard Vacuum Oil Company/4:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sokobin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-14T16:00:00+08:00">September 14, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 14—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to my telegram of September 11, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d362-f1"/> junks destroyed by Japanese warship carried no oil.
                    However, shipment <pb facs="0335" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/> of American oil on 5
                    junks arrived safely with exception of 114 cases of kerosene which were
                    confiscated by a Japanese warship.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sokobin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
